{
  "email": "mei.chen@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Check account and mailbox percent_used per KB-010"
}

{
  "query": "enable online archive Outlook",
  "reason": "Check for archive-specific guidance to include in user instructions"
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, I looked into this and your mailbox really is almost full. It's at about 99% of its 50 GB limit, which is why Outlook keeps warning you and some emails won't send. Clearing some space will fix it. Here's how:\n\n1. Empty your Deleted Items and Junk Email folders. Right-click each one and choose Empty Folder.\n2. In your Inbox and Sent Items, sort by Size (largest first). Delete the big emails you don't need. For attachments you want to keep, save them to OneDrive first, then delete the email.\n3. If you need to keep older mail, use the Online Archive and move mail older than a year into it. Let us know if you don't see an Online Archive folder in Outlook.\n\nAfter you clean up, your mailbox size can take up to an hour to update. Then you should be able to send normally again. If you're still over 95% after cleaning up and your work really needs more space, reply here. A bigger mailbox needs your manager's approval, and we can start that for you.",
  "internal_note": "Checked the account: Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst). Mailbox is at 50890 of 51200 MB (99.4%), so it's very close to the 100% point where sending stops. That matches the warnings and the emails that won't send. The account itself is fine: active, 0 failed sign-ins, not blocked. I gave her the KB-010 cleanup steps (empty Deleted Items and Junk, sort by size and move attachments to OneDrive, Online Archive for mail older than a year, then wait up to an hour for the size to update). Not escalated: KB-010 only calls for that if she's still over 95% after cleanup and her role needs a larger quota, which needs manager approval.\n\nTECHNICIAN ACTION NEEDED: I queued an unlock_account request for user_id 9 by mistake (pending approval id 1). Please reject it. The account isn't locked and doesn't need unlocking.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
